e solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the \n{{field-3}} \nSince ${e}^{3t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/98/98fc60d566b520f3d943e42ee8f4e07aa0bdd33b53fbb04981c2e8f4001210fd.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.11$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $0.22$ | $1$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/ee/eed535cfbba657a10aa37ffd90c4de36ae85e5acfa6e44b1790ec3372da10c3c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/4e/4eaab4510bb15a7207aedaf37bff252132f62550d5dc62373aea0b506b7b0611.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =3$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =3,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{3t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{3t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward $\\text{infinity}$ in the phase plane as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/98/98fc60d566b520f3d943e42ee8f4e07aa0bdd33b53fbb04981c2e8f4001210fd.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{3t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{3t} \\\\ y={e}^{3t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.11$ | $0$ | $2.24$ |\n| $y$ | $0.22$ | $1$ | $4.48$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/ee/eed535cfbba657a10aa37ffd90c4de36ae85e5acfa6e44b1790ec3372da10c3c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/4e/4eaab4510bb15a7207aedaf37bff252132f62550d5dc62373aea0b506b7b0611.png)"} :step/id #uuid "61cf691b-d2b0-5082-860e-8f5caf14e159"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551441 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551331 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4607cf6e-3e20-5e09-a1a5-531194df6bd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550530} {:answer/id #uuid "6f2c1230-c00c-51e9-ae67-b1cccc809e43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550647} {:answer/id #uuid "a9e99b2a-d27b-529d-91f0-fdfda3691a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4.95" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550818} {:answer/id #uuid "c4648e3f-2e11-59eb-8f00-3010f5c082be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550898}] :