6045485} :question/id #uuid "bff2c616-f045-5186-8916-8acfc055fce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-333304" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=4x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=4y(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvector corresponding to the only eigenvalue of the system's matrix $A$ is $v=[1,\\text{ }0]^{T}.$ The vector $w=[0,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ is such that $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{{field-1}}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}{{field-2}},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the \n{{field-3}} \nSince ${e}^{4t}\\to $ \n{{field-4}} \nas $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward \n{{field-5}}  \nas $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/27/27e921a76383c4f8a4fc1e81a1febcfad53f330d0e902f4e07578238da33422f.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x={{field-6}} \\\\ y={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.07$ | $0$ | {{field-7}} |\n| $y$ | $0.14$ | $1$ | {{field-8}} |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/36/36ae671944545eaae9027ef0d4a876e12ceef17d01be0ad881d32dfdcb8ad963.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/1f/1fd20f7333800323c44f41d7906958a0928d5f30279e36b1f50d0ca1f66fcd46.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a repeated eigenvalue $\\lambda =4$ (of multiplicity two) and only one corresponding eigenvector $v,$ the solution of the system is given by\n\n$$\nx(t)={c}_{1}v{e}^{\\lambda t}+{c}_{2}(vt{e}^{\\lambda t}+w{e}^{\\lambda t}\\,),\n$$\n\nwhere $w$ is a solution to the equation $(A-\\lambda I)w=v.$\n\nIn our case, \n\n$$\n\\lambda =4,\\,v=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,w=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nThus, the general solution of the system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}] & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}([\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]t{e}^{4t}+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{4t}) \\\\  & ={c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe straight-line solutions of the form\n${c}_{1}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$\nlie on the $x\\text{-axis}.$ Since ${e}^{4t}\\to \\infty $ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ these solutions move toward $\\text{infinity}$ in the phase plane as $t\\to \\infty .$\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/27/27e921a76383c4f8a4fc1e81a1febcfad53f330d0e902f4e07578238da33422f.png)\n\nNow, consider solutions of the form\n${c}_{2}{e}^{4t}[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\nWhen ${c}_{2}=1,$ we get the following curve:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=t{e}^{4t} \\\\ y={e}^{4t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nComputing the coordinates (rounded to two decimal places) of several points on the curve, we get the table below.\n\n| $t$ | $-0.5$ | $0$ | $0.4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-0.07$ | $0$ | $1.98$ |\n| $y$ | $0.14$ | $1$ | $4.95$ |\n\nLet's add the solutions to the phase space.\n\n![](images/fd/fd431b8daf3ad9c1b25225af9d64b1e4876e4e1a90e1dfd010de8ed134ae323c.png)\n\nThe phase portrait of our system looks as follows:\n\n![](images/1f/1fd20f7333800323c44f41d7906958a0928d5f30279e36b1f50d0ca1f66fcd46.png)"} :step/id #uuid "b2608a3b-a978-5a1c-83d8-9303ec15fa5d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551407}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551449 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478412 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f0014ce-f1b5-5fad-8afd-2cf5dc262c17" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3.14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477854} {:answer/id #uuid "58194cff-400a-5d0f-8ea2-50e161a05d8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2.72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477917} {:answer/id #uuid "999d3727-c5a0-561e-8da5-206c863d370c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478032} {:answer/id #uuid "ace8ef5f-0d18-5e17-95f4-e812b1935864" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "0.37" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478068}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186477917} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ebcdea7-a406-5dc7-814e-cffb9363524b" :answer-field/key "field-8" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478252} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "024e08bd-5d19-54df-95c6-50e41bb1a673" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477737} {:answer/id #uuid "1cf8bb88-cefa-5a70-a834-44ac6c506cda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477787} {:answer/id #uuid "2e361041-b290-5b7f-885c-36b5007d272e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186477818} {:answer/id #uuid "935fcb77-43f1-56a8-bfa9-b356d1f4ddb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "t{e}^{2t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186478025}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186478025} :answer-field/id #uuid "7922409b-1094-5b90-a666-97ec9d9a960a" :answer-field/key "